PHASE 3 — Service Discovery Engine

This is where the product begins becoming unique.

User enters:

"I want to sell Roblox character design"

The system creates the initial service profile.

Analyze
Main Service
    ↓
Service Category
    ↓
Sub-services
    ↓
Possible Buyer Types
    ↓
Possible Use Cases

Example:

Roblox Character Design

├── Dynamic Head
├── Furry Avatar
├── UGC Character
├── YouTube Character
├── VTuber Character
└── Game Character

At this stage, don't use AI yet.

Build the underlying structure.

PHASE 4 — Marketplace Research Engine

Now make the system understand marketplace listings.

The extension should be able to identify information from supported marketplace pages that is publicly available and permitted to access.

Extract structured information such as:

Title
Category
Tags where visible
Description
Price
Reviews where visible
Seller information where visible
Delivery time
Packages
FAQ

Store normalized research data.

Important

Do not pretend this gives you Fiverr's private search data or secret ranking algorithm.

You're analyzing observable marketplace information.

PHASE 5 — Search & Keyword Intelligence

Now build your keyword system.

Instead of simply:

"Here are 20 keywords."

Create:

Keyword hierarchy
CORE
   ↓
PRIMARY
   ↓
SECONDARY
   ↓
LONG-TAIL
   ↓
BUYER-INTENT

For example:

Roblox character
        ↓
Custom Roblox character
        ↓
Roblox furry avatar
        ↓
Roblox dynamic head
        ↓
Custom Roblox character for YouTube

Each keyword receives attributes such as:

relevance
specificity
competition signal
buyer intent
relationship to service
PHASE 6 — Buyer Intent Engine

This is one of your core features.

Instead of asking:

"What keyword is popular?"

Ask:

"What does the buyer actually want?"

Create intent categories:

GENERAL
SPECIFIC SERVICE
FEATURE
USE CASE
PROBLEM
AUDIENCE
OUTCOME
PURCHASE-READY

Example:

"Roblox character for YouTube"

could be classified as:

Audience: YouTube creator
Use case: Content creation
Service: Character design
Intent: Purchase-oriented
PHASE 7 — Root Need Engine

Now go deeper.

For every discovered search/service:

SEARCH TERM
     ↓
BUYER INTENT
     ↓
BUYER PROBLEM
     ↓
ROOT NEED
     ↓
DESIRED OUTCOME

Example:

"Roblox furry avatar"

        ↓

Wants a custom avatar

        ↓

Doesn't want a generic character

        ↓

Needs a recognizable online identity

        ↓

Wants an avatar suitable for their content/community

The interface should explain:

WHAT

What the term means.

WHY

Why a buyer might use it.

WHERE

Where the freelancer should use it.

WHO

What type of buyer it attracts.

